diff --git a/doc/man/tor.1.txt b/doc/man/tor.1.txt
index 88e09e3f40..c5e7c71632 100644
--- a/doc/man/tor.1.txt
+++ b/doc/man/tor.1.txt
@@ -3161,6 +3161,22 @@ The following options are useful only for a exit relay.
     not defined or set to 0, it is controlled by a consensus parameter. If not
     defined in the consensus, the value is 300. (Default: 0)
 
+The following options are useful only for an onion service directory (HSDir).
+
+[[HSDirRefuseUnknownPrevHop]] **HSDirRefuseUnknownPrevHop** **0**|**1**|**auto**::
+
+    Since 0.4.2.1-alpha an HSDir refuses onion service descriptor fetches and
+    uploads from client channels, so they can't be made over one-hop circuits.
+    But a peer can authenticate with any self-generated relay identity, which
+    is not a client channel. If set to 1, an HSDir refuses (with a 503) such a
+    request whose previous hop is not a relay in its consensus or for which it
+    has a descriptor; if 0, it only counts them. "auto" means use the
+    hsdir_refuse_unknown_prev_hop consensus parameter, and only count if the
+    consensus is silent. This option, and that parameter, are independent of
+    RefuseUnknownExits, so turning this off does not weaken exit protection.
+    The count appears in the heartbeat and as
+    tor_relay_dos_total{type="hsdir_unknown_prev_hop"}. (Default: auto)
+
 
 For onion services, mitigations are a work in progress and multiple options
 are currently available.
